     "problem_md": "Solve  $30+2x=3(3-4x)$.\n\n$x$ = ................................................",
     "solution_md": "*\"Solve\" means to get *$x=...$* (with no *$x$* terms on the right-hand side)* \n*Expand the brackets (by multiplying everything inside them by 3)* * *\n\n$30+2x=9-12x$\n\n**[1]**\n\n*Get the *$x$* terms on one side (by adding *$12x$* to both sides and collecting like terms)* * *\n\n`table attributes columnalign right center left columnspacing 0px end attributes row cell 30 plus 2 x plus 12 x end cell equals 9 row cell 30 plus 14 x end cell equals 9 end table` * *\n\n*Get the *$14x$* term on its own (by subtracting 30 from both sides)* * *\n\n$14x=9-30\\,14x=-21$\n\n**[1]**\n\n*Get *$x$* on its own (by dividing both sides by 14)* * *\n\n$x=\\frac{-21}{14}=-1.5$\n\n**-1.5**** ****[1]** \n**The answer as a fraction, **$-\\frac{3}{2}$**, is also accepted**",
