     "part_tier": null,
     "problem_md": "Solve the equation $\\frac{2x+5}{3-x}=\\frac{14}{15}$.\n\n$x=$................................................",
     "solution_md": "> *Get rid of the fractions by multiplying both sides by the denominators. Use brackets around expressions when multiplying.*\n\n`table row cell fraction numerator 2 x plus 5 over denominator up diagonal strike 3 minus x end strike end fraction cross times up diagonal strike open parentheses 3 minus x close parentheses end strike cross times 15 end cell equals cell fraction numerator 14 over denominator up diagonal strike 15 end fraction cross times open parentheses 3 minus x close parentheses cross times up diagonal strike 15 end cell row cell open parentheses 2 x plus 5 close parentheses cross times 15 end cell equals cell 14 cross times open parentheses 3 minus x close parentheses end cell row cell 15 open parentheses 2 x plus 5 close parentheses end cell equals cell 14 open parentheses 3 minus x close parentheses end cell end table`\n\n**[1]**\n\n> *Expand both brackets.*\n\n$30x+75=42-14x$\n\n**[1]**\n\n*Get all the **x** terms on one side.* \n*Add 14**x** to both sides.*\n\n`table row cell 30 x plus 75 plus 14 x end cell equals 42 row cell 44 x plus 75 end cell equals 42 end table`\n\n*Get the **x **term alone on one side.* \n*Subtract 75 from both sides.*\n\n$44x=42-75\\,44x=-33$\n\n> *Divide both sides by 44.*\n\n$x=-\\frac{33}{44}$\n\n> *Simplify the fraction.*\n\n$x=-\\frac{3}{4}$* ***[1] **\n**It is also acceptable to write as a decimal: **$x=-0.75$",
     "equations": [
      {
       "latex": "\\frac{2x+5}{3-x}=\\frac{14}{15}",
