     "problem_md": "Solve the equation.\n\n$3(x-4)+\\frac{x+2}{5}=6$\n\n$x$ = ..............................................",
     "solution_md": "> *Multiply both sides by 5, remember to apply this to every term*\n\n`15 open parentheses x minus 4 close parentheses plus open parentheses x plus 2 close parentheses equals 30`\n\n**[1]**\n\n> *Expand the bracket on the left*\n\n`15 x minus 60 plus open parentheses x plus 2 close parentheses equals 30`\n\n> *Simplify the left*\n\n$16x-58=30$\n\n**[1]**\n\n> *Add 58 to both sides*\n\n$16x=88$\n\n**[1]**\n\n> *Divide both sides by 16*\n\n$x=\\frac{88}{16}=\\frac{11}{2}=5.5$\n\n$x=5.5$ **[1]** \n**Or as a fraction **$\\frac{11}{2}$",
     "equations": [
      {
